[{:seon.task/name "each-run-teaches-the-next"
  :seon.task/plan "Learn from every run automatically, without regressions, slowdown or growth (DECISIONS: every live run better than the last). Reproduction: the first DeepSeek agent on Seon's code (`seon.reconcile/a-refused-spawn-is-recorded`) spent 8 turns and 59 errors without a fix; the causes were readable only by querying its branch's evaluation records: `clojure.repl/source` failing for platform vars, `slurp` of repository files not found, guessed namespaces. What exists: `seon.learn/waste` charges a run's wasted forms to the context producer that led to them, and the judge records it (`:seon.task/waste`, the agent's own `:seon.agent/waste`, `seon.reconcile/judge-tx`, class `:waste` in `seon.problems`). Correct, extending that and adding nothing beside it: the record answers \"what did this run lack\": its failed forms grouped by kind (an unresolved var or namespace, no source, file not found, a contract's error, a wrong arity), each with its count and one example, and the names it tried to read that its context did not show. `my.root/problems` ranks the lacks of every run on main by kind, most frequent first, one example each, so the next fix is the commonest gap across a steady stream of new real tasks (no matrix of reruns). The agent's instructions (the help page, `docs/agent.md`) name today's functions (`my.schema/register!`, `source`), each resolving. Budget: about 120 net src lines; no new namespace; nothing on the turn's hot path beyond the fold at the run's end. (`seon.turn/context-block` already takes gaps since the merge base.)"
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/a-run-records-what-it-lacked
                      seon.problems-test/lacks-are-ranked-across-runs
                      seon.context-test/the-server-context-shows-only-new-contract-gaps}}
 {:seon.task/name "turns-to-green-report"
  :seon.task/plan "The owner's key number: turns to a good solution, from all runs (AGENTS §1). What exists: :seon.agent/turn, :seon.model-call/tokens, cache-hit-tokens and cache-miss-tokens, and :seon.task/waste are recorded; `seon.learn` has `waste` and `summary` only, and nothing reports turns to green. v1: `seon.mine` and ``my.root/turns-report`` (median and p90 per step, model and commit; ~/src/seon/src/seon/mine.clj:544-729). Correct: `seon.learn/report`, one query: median and p90 turns to green per template (step), per model and per main commit; tokens and cost per green; cache-hit share; the top waste rules. It renders on its schema on the dashboard and in root's context (`seon.render.ai/system`)."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.learn-test/report-quantiles-match-recorded-runs}}]
